    dcterms:source "Book of the Dead, chapter 125, the address to the forty-two gods, address 28, Papyrus of Ani, in the transliteration and English of E. A. Wallis Budge, London: British Museum, 1895, plates XXXI-XXXII, pp. 198-203",
        "Budge, A Hieroglyphic Vocabulary to the Theban Recension of the Book of the Dead, London: Kegan Paul, 1911, s.v. An-hetep, p. 48" ;
    skos:definition "The twenty-eighth address of chapter 125 in the Papyrus of Ani. Budge renders the name bringer of his offering. The god is addressed as coming forth from Sau, and the address is bound to one denial: I have not acted insolently."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BookOfTheDead ;
    pm:nameForm "an-hetep" ;
