    pm:fromWork pmw:BookOfTheDead ;
    pm:nameForm "qererti" ;
    pm:nameRole "one of the forty-two gods of the hall of the two Maati" ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:EgyptianRitual .

pmc:AegyptiaRereti a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Rereti"@de,
        "Rereti"@en ;
    dcterms:source "Book of the Dead, chapter 125, the address to the forty-two gods, address 6, Papyrus of Ani, in the transliteration and English of E. A. Wallis Budge, London: British Museum, 1895, plates XXXI-XXXII, pp. 198-203",
        "Budge, A Hieroglyphic Vocabulary to the Theban Recension of the Book of the Dead, London: Kegan Paul, 1911, s.v. Rerti (?), p. 239" ;
    skos:altLabel "Rerti (Vocabulary, 1911)"@en ;
    skos:definition "The sixth address of chapter 125 in the Papyrus of Ani. Budge renders the name double lion-god. The god is addressed as coming forth from pet, the heaven, and the address is bound to one denial: I have not diminished the oblations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BookOfTheDead ;
