pmc:EuropeanFolkMagicZeugnisBingemanBube a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Johann Bingemans Bube, Ruscombmanor, Spätjahr 1812"@de,
        "Johann Bingeman's boy, Ruscombmanor, autumn 1812"@en ;
    dcterms:source "Johann Georg Hohman, Der lange verborgene Freund (Reading, Pa., 1820), Abschnitt »Zeugniße«",
        "John George Hohman, The Long Lost Friend (Harrisburg, Pa., 1850), p. 6" ;
    skos:note "Attested as a third-party ascription and not as a first-person report, because the author did not perform it. The acting person is his wife, and he reports what she did. The section holds two such cases and thirteen of his own, and the difference is kept rather than levelled."@en,
        "The boy had burnt himself severely and mortification had already set in. The author's wife came there by chance in the late autumn of eighteen twelve, used for it, and the mortification was driven out in a short time; the boy was soon restored and healed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:EuropeanFolkMagicGebrauchen ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HohmanFreund1820,
        pmw:HohmanLongLostFriend1850 ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:EuropeanFolkMagic ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:EuropeanFolkMagicKalterBrandVertreibung .

