pmc:EuropeanFolkMagicZeugnisStaufer a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Jacob Staufers Kind am Heckack, Bucks Caunty"@de,
        "Jacob Staufer's child at the Heckack, Bucks County"@en ;
    dcterms:source "Johann Georg Hohman, Der lange verborgene Freund (Reading, Pa., 1820), Abschnitt »Zeugniße«",
        "John George Hohman, The Long Lost Friend (Harrisburg, Pa., 1850), pp. 7-8" ;
    skos:note "A small child that had the fits every hour. The author sold Staufer a book containing the twenty-five letters; on the urging of his neighbour Henrich Franckenfeld, Staufer used the twenty-five letters, and the child was at once freed of the fits and became well. The same letters, the author adds, are in this book too."@en,
        "The only case in the section that names the means, the only one performed by the sufferer's own household rather than by the author, and the only one with a second named person as the mover. It is therefore the strongest of the fifteen for the transmission's own claim, since the book worked in a hand that was not its author's."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:EuropeanFolkMagicGebrauchen ;
